  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VISAYAS BASE-LOAD POWER PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project involves construction and operation of a 200- megawatt (MW) coal-fired power plant in Naga City, Cebu, in the Visayas region. The plant is needed to address the power shortage in the region, and will adopt a more environment-friendly technology by using circulating fluidized bed (CFB) combustion boilers. It will provide base-load power to the grid. CFB is the next best solution to using pulverized coal technology. Supercritical technology cannot be used for a 200 MW plant.</narrative>
  </description>
